Isotope: GTK's window button layout follows window_controls_left.

What: src/theme.rs builds the GTK `button-layout` string in a pure function,
`gnome_button_layout`, and mirrors it when the CosmicTk key
`window_controls_left` (added by patches/cosmic/libcosmic) is true:
`close,minimize,maximize:`, `close,maximize:`, `close,minimize:`, `close:`.
Upstream's right layout is unchanged when the key is false. The layout is set
at start and again when show_maximize, show_minimize or window_controls_left
changes. A unit test covers all eight cases.

Why: at startup and on those changes cosmic-settings-daemon runs `gsettings set
org.gnome.desktop.wm.preferences button-layout ':minimize,maximize,close'`.
Isotope has no dconf, so GLib uses its keyfile backend and the value lands in
~/.config/glib-2.0/settings/keyfile, which overrides the schema default
`close,minimize,maximize:` of 91_isotope-cosmic.gschema.override. Flatpak and
GTK apps (through xdg-desktop-portal-gtk) then got the buttons on the right
while COSMIC's own windows had them on the left.

Made against cosmic-settings-daemon epoch-1.11.0 (libcosmic 430f3d48a97d, the
revision the libcosmic patch applies to).

